Recall the Fibonacci recurrence \(F_{n+2}=F_{n+1}+F_n\).  Then

\[
\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_nF_{n+2}}
   =\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n(F_{n+1}+F_n)}
   =\frac{1}{F_n}-\frac{1}{F_{n+2}} .
\]

Hence the series telescopes:

\[
\begin{aligned}
\sum_{n=1}^{N}\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_nF_{n+2}}
&=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigl(\frac{1}{F_n}-\frac{1}{F_{n+2}}\Bigr) \\
&=\Bigl(\frac{1}{F_1}+\frac{1}{F_2}\Bigr)-\Bigl(\frac{1}{F_{N+1}}+\frac{1}{F_{N+2}}\Bigr).
\end{aligned}
\]

Since \(F_n\to\infty\) as \(n\to\infty\), the last two terms vanish in the limit.  Using \(F_1=F_2=1\),

\[
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_nF_{n+2}}
= \frac{1}{1}+\frac{1}{1}=2.
\]

