The robot’s speed is  

\[
\frac{1\text{ km}}{2.5\text{ h}}=\frac{1000\text{ m}}{2.5\text{ h}}
      =400\text{ m/h}.
\]

Convert to meters per second:

\[
400\text{ m/h}\times\frac{1\text{ h}}{3600\text{ s}}
   =\frac{400}{3600}\text{ m/s}
   =\frac{1}{9}\text{ m/s}.
\]

The hallway is traversed in \(90\) seconds, so its length is

\[
\text{distance}= \text{speed}\times\text{time}
   =\frac{1}{9}\text{ m/s}\times 90\text{ s}
   =10\text{ m}.
\]

